Core Pokémon games are turn-based RPGs where players catch creatures and battle trainers. Key mechanics include catching Pokémon with Poké Balls, training teams, leveling up, and type advantages in battles. Each generation introduces "flagship mechanics": Generation VI (X/Y) added Mega Evolution (temporary powerful transformations); Generation VII (Sun/Moon) featured Z-Moves (enhanced one-per-battle moves); Generation VIII (Sword/Shield) introduced Dynamax (size boost with 3-turn limit and stat boosts). New Legends games (Z-A, Arceus) shifted to real-time battles instead of turn-based. Games released across Nintendo handhelds: Game Boy, DS, 3DS, Switch. Over 500 million game units sold lifetime, with Scarlet/Violet (2022) selling 26+ million copies.